WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.139
Dashboards for Indigo. Here is a look round a real house. Everything you see is live, and every press is real.

2
00:00:09.839 --> 00:00:17.263
This is the hub, the page that lives on the wall tablet. It answers one question first: is the house all right?

3
00:00:17.713 --> 00:00:24.027
The pills say who is home, how many radiators are calling for heat, and whether anything needs a look.

4
00:00:24.477 --> 00:00:28.019
Favourites are one-tap tiles. Press the garage door,

5
00:00:28.469 --> 00:00:32.714
and the tile turns blue and counts the seconds while the door moves.

6
00:00:34.919 --> 00:00:40.529
It turns red once the door is fully open, and the live camera strip shows it happening.

7
00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:50.591
Every room has its own page. The garage has its cameras, and the door, which is open now.

8
00:00:51.041 --> 00:00:55.137
Press to close, and the tile follows the door all the way down.

9
00:00:55.587 --> 00:00:59.470
It goes quiet again once the sensors say the door is shut.

10
00:01:14.137 --> 00:01:16.271
Tap any camera on the hub,

11
00:01:17.371 --> 00:01:21.317
and the Cameras page opens with every camera playing live.

12
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:27.463
The big picture follows whichever one you tap. Tap the front door, and it swaps to the top.

13
00:01:31.317 --> 00:01:38.379
Further down the hub are the power flow, today's solar and the weather station. More on the energy in a moment.

14
00:01:38.829 --> 00:01:41.303
Rooms lists every room in the house.

15
00:01:46.729 --> 00:01:49.310
In the kitchen, switch the spot lights on,

16
00:01:50.179 --> 00:01:52.803
and slide them down to half brightness.

17
00:01:53.629 --> 00:01:56.487
All On switches on every light in the room.

18
00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:03.668
A room can leave a light out of that group, such as a main light that keeps its own switch.

19
00:02:04.118 --> 00:02:06.529
And All Off puts them all out again.

20
00:02:08.818 --> 00:02:15.901
Heating shows every radiator with its temperature and its setpoint, and a boost for the whole house at the top.

21
00:02:16.351 --> 00:02:25.119
We are still in summer mode here, so every radiator is held at eight degrees. The boost comes into its own once the heating is needed again.

22
00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:34.349
The sun has gone for the day, so the battery is powering the house, from 43 percent, and selling the spare to the grid.

23
00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:42.261
The dots show which way the power is going, and they speed up as more of it flows.

24
00:02:42.711 --> 00:02:53.655
Underneath are how self-sufficient the house has been today, 72 percent so far, the solar against today's forecast, what it has saved in pounds, and the battery's charge.

25
00:02:54.161 --> 00:03:03.142
Each hour's solar is split by roof, and set against a dashed mark for what the forecast promised. The pale bars are the hours still to come.

26
00:03:03.592 --> 00:03:12.168
The battery section shows what it is doing now, its last day as a line, and its health, down to the temperature and balance of the cells.

27
00:03:12.618 --> 00:03:16.778
And When to run it plans the washing around the sun and the battery.

28
00:03:18.478 --> 00:03:23.043
Scenes puts every Indigo action group on a button, grouped by folder.

29
00:03:24.743 --> 00:03:31.762
Alerts gathers the errors in Indigo's log, and lets you add your own rules, sent by Pushover or email.

30
00:03:33.462 --> 00:03:41.697
WiFi shows every access point and every client, and flags a crowded channel or an old device slowing the rest down.

31
00:03:43.397 --> 00:03:50.031
And Mains lists every meter in the house, with how far they disagree with each other and with the inverter.

32
00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:57.577
Dashboards is free and open source. Take the parts that suit your house, and leave the rest.
